WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.996
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for the two letters that get mixed up.

2
00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:05.155
These two.

3
00:00:07.517 --> 00:00:11.762
This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

4
00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:16.705
This plan is for a child who knows the letters, but mixes up these two.

5
00:00:17.155 --> 00:00:18.447
Sometimes when reading.

6
00:00:18.897 --> 00:00:21.099
Sometimes when they write. Often both.

7
00:00:21.549 --> 00:00:26.209
It is common before the age of seven. It is not a sign that something is wrong.

8
00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:33.809
A cup is a cup whichever way it faces. Letters are the first things that change their name when they are turned around.

9
00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:39.114
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

10
00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:47.475
Day one is a short check. It shows you where the mix-up is: in reading, in writing, or both. Day ten shows you what changed.

11
00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:53.182
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

12
00:00:53.632 --> 00:00:56.972
And there are three helpers. Your child learns one at a time.

13
00:00:57.672 --> 00:01:01.449
Helper one. To write this letter, draw the bat first, then the ball.

14
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:07.680
Helper two. To write this letter, make the round part first. Then go up, and down.

15
00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:15.741
Helper three. The word bed looks like a bed. The first letter is the head of the bed. The last letter is the foot.

16
00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:23.644
Now, what to expect. One letter at a time. Day two is only the first letter. Day three is only the other one.

17
00:01:24.094 --> 00:01:29.232
They meet on day four. Teaching both together from the start is what keeps them mixed up.

18
00:01:29.682 --> 00:01:34.515
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

19
00:01:34.965 --> 00:01:42.128
This plan is practice in the right order. It is not a promise. On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

20
00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:49.415
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

21
00:01:49.865 --> 00:01:54.433
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

22
00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:58.031
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

23
00:01:58.481 --> 00:02:02.550
Then your child carries on with the page, and shows you three things at the end.

24
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.879
On three of the days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

25
00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:12.868
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and a red and a blue crayon.

26
00:02:13.318 --> 00:02:18.530
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about three minutes.
